      "start_seconds": 1.23,
      "end_seconds": 4.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "hello, come in mind the step"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.61,
      "end_seconds": 6.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "hi there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.73,
      "end_seconds": 10.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "What's been worrying you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.37,
      "end_seconds": 23.24,
      "duration_seconds": 11.87,
      "text": "Doctor, it's a productive cough with rusty phlegm. It's getting on my nerves now. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.75,
      "end_seconds": 27.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Is there any regular medication you use?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.5,
      "end_seconds": 35.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "No, I don't take any tablets."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.2,
      "end_seconds": 55.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.56,
      "end_seconds": 60.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "I've had it for two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.78,
      "end_seconds": 66.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "and and what about leg swelling, recent travel or confusion?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.23,
      "end_seconds": 70.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "No, not a a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.82,
      "end_seconds": 73.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.55,
      "end_seconds": 78.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "No, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.88,
      "end_seconds": 94.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "alright, a few questions about your lifestyle now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.56,
      "end_seconds": 112.55,
      "duration_seconds": 16.99,
      "text": "Nothing, I'm teetotal. I gave up cigarettes last spring. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. I do a yoga class on Thursdays. Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.91,
      "end_seconds": 117.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.53,
      "end_seconds": 123.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "Okay, so no, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.15,
      "end_seconds": 129.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "do you have any medical conditions I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.87,
      "end_seconds": 131.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "no, no conditions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.74,
      "end_seconds": 135.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.99,
      "end_seconds": 147.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.51,
      "end_seconds": 171.84,
      "duration_seconds": 8.33,
      "text": "Okay: pressure 112 over 77, saturation 98 percent. And heart rate 93, temperature 38.3, respiratory rate 17."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.96,
      "end_seconds": 176.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.87,
      "end_seconds": 179.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.19,
      "end_seconds": 201.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.16,
      "text": "There are crackles at the right base and the breathing is a bit fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.72,
      "end_seconds": 218.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.01,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.03,
      "end_seconds": 223.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "good, you can sit up again"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.69,
      "end_seconds": 246.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "taking everything into account, the most likely explanation is community-acquired pneumonia"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.04,
      "end_seconds": 251.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.24,
      "end_seconds": 266.19,
      "duration_seconds": 12.95,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now community-acquired pneumonia is my leading thought, not anything worse. A chest X-ray is what I'd like next, for possible pneumonia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.21,
      "end_seconds": 269.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "okay, I'll do it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.06,
      "end_seconds": 274.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "I'm going to order blood tests, for pneumonia"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.13,
      "end_seconds": 279.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "okay, so how long will it take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.16,
      "end_seconds": 312.13,
      "duration_seconds": 30.97,
      "text": "what I'm giving you is amoxicillin, 500 milligrams, three times a day, five days it's for chest infection rest, drink plenty, and come back if you are not improving in two days keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency come back in one week does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 313.19,
      "end_seconds": 316.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.31,
      "end_seconds": 320.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Take care now."
    }
  ]
}